<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Addis Ababa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Addis Ababa is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, founded in the late nineteenth century under Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>. It became the political and administrative centre of the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>. Italian forces occupied the city in 1936, making it the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-east-africa">Italian East Africa</a> until Ethiopian and British forces liberated it in 1941.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/addis-ababa.jpg" alt="Addis Ababa" width="320" height="198" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abshewaga · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Addis_in_night.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
